Generates and manages the app's `OpenTofu` infrastructure

Usage: leptoskit infra <COMMAND>

Commands:
  analytics  Queries read-only JSON evidence from one app instance, not a fleet total
  plugins    Prints the versioned capability catalog, enabled plugins and bindings as JSON
  build      Builds the server/website image with migration metadata; optionally pushes it
  generate   Writes inspectable main.tf.json and deployment instructions
  plan       Initializes `OpenTofu` and saves an infrastructure plan. Does not apply it
  apply      Applies the saved plan, refusing configuration changes since planning
  prepare    Prepares private services and the backup worker without starting an app or taking an initial backup. Use before disaster recovery
  output     Prints public endpoints and the server address as JSON. Omits secrets
  releases   Lists successful releases from the primary host's shared history
  status     Reports application containers, the database, backups, and operation owner
  offers     Lists current x86 offers from providers with configured credentials, sorted by currency and base monthly price. Never provisions resources
  ci         Writes a push-to-deploy GitHub Actions workflow for a prepared Linux runner with Docker, Rust, lk, `OpenTofu`, Kamal, and an SSH agent
  backups    Encrypted scheduled backups and isolated restore checks
  restore    Restores a verified snapshot, retaining the previous database and leaving all app containers stopped. Recover its recorded image afterward
  unlock     Releases a stale operation lock after checking that its runner has stopped
  stop       Stops app containers and their workers, retaining Postgres and the tunnel. Use before explicitly rolling back the database
  publish    Publishes an already signed code-push release to the provisioned bucket
  backup     Writes a consistent Postgres custom-format backup. Copy it off-site
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
